{%- comment -%}
  Shared cart footer — the inner content of #CartFooterInner.

  Rendered by BOTH:
    - snippets/cart-drawer.liquid  (initial paint, in theme.liquid)
    - sections/cart-items.liquid   (Section Rendering API refresh)

  Both callers own the #CartFooterInner wrapper themselves, because the JS in
  theme.liquid swaps innerHTML between them. Keep this snippet wrapper-free.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Two unrelated facts. Shipping being calculated at checkout is always true, so it
    is not gated; only the VAT line follows the merchant's VAT toggle. They used to
    share one string and one switch, so turning VAT off also hid the shipping note.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if settings.show_vat_note -%}
    <p class="cart-drawer__tax-note">{{ settings.vat_note_text }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
  <p class="cart-drawer__tax-note">{{ 'cart.shipping_at_checkout' | t }}</p>
  <div class="cart-drawer__subtotal">
    <span>{{ 'cart.subtotal' | t }}</span>
    <span>{{ cart.total_price | money }}</span>
  </div>
  <a href="{{ routes.checkout_url }}" class="btn btn--primary btn--full btn--lg">{{ 'cart.checkout' | t }}</a>
  <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" class="btn btn--secondary btn--full mt-4" style="display:flex;">{{ 'cart.view_cart' | t }}</a>
{%- endif -%}
